<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-AIR BALTIC TO STOP MINSK FLIGHTS.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-AIR BALTIC TO STOP MINSK FLIGHTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airline Air Baltic said on Monday that it was stop flying to Minsk from April due to low demand on the route.</p>
<p>The airline said in a statement that fewer passengers were going to Belarus not only with Latvian airlines but also with other European airlines.</p>
<p>&quot;The airline is carefully following and analysing changes in demand and is prepared to start to flying to Minsk as soon as conditions allow it,&quot; the airline added.</p>
<p>Air Baltic is around one-third owned by Scandinavian Airlines.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
